{title: Great Is Thy Faithfulness}
{key: G}
{time: 3/4}
{+pdf.diagrams.show: right}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[G]Great is Thy [C]faithfulness, [D]O God my [G]Father!
[C]There is no [G]shadow of [A]turning with [D]Thee
[D7]Thou changest [G]not, Thy com[**]passions, they [Am]fail not
[Gdim]As Thou hast [G]been Thou fo[D]rever wilt [G]be!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[D]Great is Thy [G]faithfulness, [E7]great is Thy [Am]Faithfulness
[D]Morning by [G]morning, new [A]mercies I [D]see
[D7]All I have [G]needed, Thy [**]hand hath pro[Am]vided
[Gdim]Great is Thy [G]faithfulness, [D]Lord unto [G]me!
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[G]Summer and [C]winter, and [D]springtime and [G]harvest
[C]Sun, moon, and [G]stars in their [A]courses a[D]bove
[D7]Join with all [G]nature in [**]manifold [Am]witness
[Gdim]To Thy great [G]faithfulness, [D]mercy, and [G]love.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[G]Pardon for [C]sin and a [D]peace that en[G]dureth
[C]Thine own dear [G]presence to [A]cheer and to [D]guide
[D7]Strength for to[G]day and bright [**]hope for to[Am]morrow
[Gdim]Blessings all [G]mine, with ten [D]thousand be[G]side!
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
